1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,966
Dad's FD was growing every year,

2
00:00:04,966 --> 00:00:09,310
yet Dad was getting poorer.

3
00:00:09,310 --> 00:00:14,276
There's a thick file of receipts in the cupboard.

4
00:00:14,276 --> 00:00:18,000
Interest is written on every receipt.

5
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:24,828
Dad touches it fondly and says, son, it's safe,

6
00:00:24,828 --> 00:00:26,690
it won't go anywhere.

7
00:00:26,690 --> 00:00:30,560
One evening Mummy came home with a bag of vegetables.

8
00:00:30,560 --> 00:00:34,860
The bag was light, but the bill was heavy. Mummy said,

9
00:00:34,860 --> 00:00:39,160
this same money used to last the whole week comfortably before.

10
00:00:39,160 --> 00:00:43,460
Now it's finished by mid-week. Dad took off his glasses,

11
00:00:43,460 --> 00:00:45,180
and went quiet.

12
00:00:45,180 --> 00:00:52,236
Dad's calculation was perfectly simple. The money is in the bank,

13
00:00:52,236 --> 00:00:59,292
interest gets added every year, so the total is growing.

14
00:00:59,292 --> 00:01:03,526
The number on the receipt kept getting bigger.

15
00:01:03,526 --> 00:01:09,171
But at the shop, that same number kept getting smaller.

16
00:01:09,171 --> 00:01:14,110
This is the hidden thief in this story.

17
00:01:14,110 --> 00:01:21,179
So today, three questions. First, you get interest on an FD,

18
00:01:21,179 --> 00:01:26,127
so how did the money still shrink? Second,

19
00:01:26,127 --> 00:01:33,903
when and how much tax is cut on FD interest? Third,

20
00:01:33,903 --> 00:01:37,438
where should you keep your emergency money?

21
00:01:37,438 --> 00:01:43,800
The answers to all three are in this house's story.

22
00:01:43,800 --> 00:01:50,982
First question. You got interest, so how did the money still shrink?

23
00:01:50,982 --> 00:01:56,728
For this, you need to understand one word: inflation.

24
00:01:56,728 --> 00:02:03,192
Inflation means prices of things slowly going up.

25
00:02:03,192 --> 00:02:07,501
The thali you buy today,

26
00:02:07,501 --> 00:02:11,810
next year the same thali will cost more.

27
00:02:11,810 --> 00:02:14,906
Now look at the FD interest.

28
00:02:14,906 --> 00:02:23,576
In July 2026, banks gave an average of about 5.9 percent interest on new FDs.

29
00:02:23,576 --> 00:02:28,531
This is in a Grip Invest report.

30
00:02:28,531 --> 00:02:34,104
It sounds good. The money is growing,

31
00:02:34,104 --> 00:02:37,820
so everything is fine, right?

32
00:02:37,820 --> 00:02:41,881
But the real question is this. How much did your money grow,

33
00:02:41,881 --> 00:02:45,040
and how much did your expenses grow? If the cost of milk,

34
00:02:45,040 --> 00:02:49,553
medicine and school fees rises faster than the interest,

35
00:02:49,553 --> 00:02:52,260
then the number on the receipt is bigger,

36
00:02:52,260 --> 00:02:55,870
but your buying power has become smaller.

37
00:02:55,870 --> 00:02:58,154
This is called real return.

38
00:02:58,154 --> 00:03:03,104
Real return means what you truly have left after subtracting inflation from the interest.

39
00:03:03,104 --> 00:03:05,769
If inflation is lower than 5.9 percent,

40
00:03:05,769 --> 00:03:08,815
then you are a little ahead. If it's higher,

41
00:03:08,815 --> 00:03:11,480
So you are quietly falling behind.

42
00:03:11,480 --> 00:03:16,890
One day, the son counted the coins in his piggy bank.

43
00:03:16,890 --> 00:03:22,301
Grandfather, meaning Papa, said, don't spend them, save them.

44
00:03:22,301 --> 00:03:24,706
The son asked, Grandfather,

45
00:03:24,706 --> 00:03:30,116
the toffee that you could buy with these coins last year,

46
00:03:30,116 --> 00:03:34,324
why can't you buy it now? Papa laughed,

47
00:03:34,324 --> 00:03:37,330
but the question was absolutely right.

48
00:03:37,330 --> 00:03:42,657
Inflation is a hidden tax. Nobody fills out a form,

49
00:03:42,657 --> 00:03:45,024
no notice comes.

50
00:03:45,024 --> 00:03:51,535
Every year, your rupee just loses a little of its value.

51
00:03:51,535 --> 00:03:57,453
If the FD interest doesn't run faster than this thief,

52
00:03:57,453 --> 00:04:02,780
then the money looks safe, but keeps shrinking.

53
00:04:02,780 --> 00:04:08,932
This was never written in Papa's file.

54
00:04:08,932 --> 00:04:13,406
The receipt only tells you the interest, it doesn't tell you the inflation.

55
00:04:13,406 --> 00:04:17,880
That's why Papa felt everything was growing.

56
00:04:17,880 --> 00:04:25,710
In reality, his FD was just running to stay in the same place.

57
00:04:25,710 --> 00:04:31,086
Second question, and here is another hidden cost.

58
00:04:31,086 --> 00:04:34,671
FD interest is not free.

59
00:04:34,671 --> 00:04:38,255
It gets added to your income.

60
00:04:38,255 --> 00:04:44,826
And income is taxed, according to your slab.

61
00:04:44,826 --> 00:04:50,800
Slab means a step of income, the higher the step, the more the tax.

62
00:04:50,800 --> 00:04:55,830
My sister came home from the office and opened her FD statement on her phone.

63
00:04:55,830 --> 00:04:59,945
The interest was credited, but not in full. She asked,

64
00:04:59,945 --> 00:05:03,146
why did less come? The answer was TDS.

65
00:05:03,146 --> 00:05:09,090
TDS means the bank itself cuts your tax and sends it to the government.

66
00:05:09,090 --> 00:05:13,900
My sister thought this was the whole tax. But that's not necessarily so.

67
00:05:13,900 --> 00:05:16,523
TDS is only an advance deduction.

68
00:05:16,523 --> 00:05:20,021
The final calculation is done in the income tax return.

69
00:05:20,021 --> 00:05:22,207
If your slab is high,

70
00:05:22,207 --> 00:05:26,580
then you may have to pay more tax when filing your return.

71
00:05:26,580 --> 00:05:30,732
Now think about the highest slab.

72
00:05:30,732 --> 00:05:38,343
In the new regime, the highest slab has 30 percent tax.

73
00:05:38,343 --> 00:05:45,263
That means 30 percent of the FD interest goes to the government.

74
00:05:45,263 --> 00:05:51,490
The interest that was already fighting inflation,

75
00:05:51,490 --> 00:05:54,950
became even thinner.

76
00:05:54,950 --> 00:05:59,634
So this is the real calculation of an FD. First the tax is cut,

77
00:05:59,634 --> 00:06:01,976
then inflation eats into it. Whatever is left,

78
00:06:01,976 --> 00:06:05,723
only that is the money you have truly earned.

79
00:06:05,723 --> 00:06:12,280
For many people, this leftover part turns out much smaller than expected.

80
00:06:12,280 --> 00:06:18,790
But not everyone pays this much tax. Papa is retired,

81
00:06:18,790 --> 00:06:21,158
Their income is low.

82
00:06:21,158 --> 00:06:26,484
Under the new regime, on income up to 12 lakh,

83
00:06:26,484 --> 00:06:30,627
after the rebate, the tax comes to zero.

84
00:06:30,627 --> 00:06:34,770
Rebate means a relief given by the government.

85
00:06:34,770 --> 00:06:39,830
So for people like Papa, the tax burden can become lighter.

86
00:06:39,830 --> 00:06:43,333
But the thief called inflation is still standing right there.

87
00:06:43,333 --> 00:06:47,226
Even if there is no tax, expenses still keep going up.

88
00:06:47,226 --> 00:06:50,340
So don't look only at tax, look at the real return.

89
00:06:50,340 --> 00:06:52,907
And one more useful thing.

90
00:06:52,907 --> 00:06:56,501
If your income is within the exemption limit,

91
00:06:56,501 --> 00:06:59,581
but the bank has deducted TDS,

92
00:06:59,581 --> 00:07:04,716
then that money can come back to you when you file your return.

93
00:07:04,716 --> 00:07:08,310
Many people never claim this.

94
00:07:08,310 --> 00:07:11,390
Their money just lies there.

95
00:07:11,390 --> 00:07:17,171
Third question. So is FD useless? Not at all.

96
00:07:17,171 --> 00:07:21,667
Everything has its own job.

97
00:07:21,667 --> 00:07:25,521
The job of an FD is less about growing money,

98
00:07:25,521 --> 00:07:29,375
and more about keeping money safe.

99
00:07:29,375 --> 00:07:36,440
And in one place, an FD does this job very well.

100
00:07:36,440 --> 00:07:42,021
One night, Papa had chest pain.

101
00:07:42,021 --> 00:07:48,299
At the hospital, the first question was, how much deposit will you pay?

102
00:07:48,299 --> 00:07:55,972
At that time, we couldn't wait for some long scheme.

103
00:07:55,972 --> 00:08:02,250
We needed the money that very night, without any delay.

104
00:08:02,250 --> 00:08:06,033
This is what we call an emergency fund.

105
00:08:06,033 --> 00:08:14,229
An emergency fund means money kept only for difficult times.

106
00:08:14,229 --> 00:08:17,382
If you lose your job, if illness comes,

107
00:08:17,382 --> 00:08:21,795
or if a sudden expense comes up at home.

108
00:08:21,795 --> 00:08:28,100
The job of this money is not to earn, but to be available on time.

109
00:08:28,100 --> 00:08:31,530
This is where an FD or a savings account is useful.

110
00:08:31,530 --> 00:08:35,390
The money can be taken out quickly, and the value doesn't go up and down.

111
00:08:35,390 --> 00:08:37,105
Inflation will eat a little, agreed.

112
00:08:37,105 --> 00:08:43,537
But the value of getting money instantly in an emergency is far more than that small loss.

113
00:08:43,537 --> 00:08:46,110
You also get to sleep peacefully at night.

114
00:08:46,110 --> 00:08:49,245
And what if the bank itself collapses?

115
00:08:49,245 --> 00:08:51,932
This is where DICGC comes in.

116
00:08:51,932 --> 00:08:55,962
DICGC is the organization that provides insurance on bank deposits.

117
00:08:55,962 --> 00:08:59,097
For each depositor, in each bank,

118
00:08:59,097 --> 00:09:02,680
cover up to 5 lakh rupees is given.

119
00:09:02,680 --> 00:09:06,190
So Wife made a simple rule for the house.

120
00:09:06,190 --> 00:09:09,310
Don't keep the whole emergency money in just one bank,

121
00:09:09,310 --> 00:09:12,040
If needed, in different banks.

122
00:09:12,040 --> 00:09:15,160
So that your money stays within the cover everywhere.

123
00:09:15,160 --> 00:09:17,890
This is not fear, it's just being sensible.

124
00:09:17,890 --> 00:09:21,531
An FD is fine for small goals too.

125
00:09:21,531 --> 00:09:23,554
Next year's school fees for the child,

126
00:09:23,554 --> 00:09:28,005
or a wedding expense a few months from now. When you need the money soon,

127
00:09:28,005 --> 00:09:32,860
taking the risk of a place that goes up and down is not sensible.

128
00:09:32,860 --> 00:09:35,942
Now, the mistake that Papa made,

129
00:09:35,942 --> 00:09:40,344
and many people make. The mistake was not taking an FD.

130
00:09:40,344 --> 00:09:41,225
The mistake was

131
00:09:41,225 --> 00:09:45,627
keeping a whole lifetime's savings only in FDs for years and years.

132
00:09:45,627 --> 00:09:50,030
Treating long-term money like emergency money too.

133
00:09:50,030 --> 00:09:56,553
Over the long run, inflation cuts a little every year.

134
00:09:56,553 --> 00:09:59,451
On top of that, tax too.

135
00:09:59,451 --> 00:10:05,974
Year after year, this small cut keeps adding up.

136
00:10:05,974 --> 00:10:13,946
And one day Mummy asks, where did the money go? The answer is,

137
00:10:13,946 --> 00:10:16,120
quietly, slowly.

138
00:10:16,120 --> 00:10:18,066
So what should we do? First step,

139
00:10:18,066 --> 00:10:21,179
divide your savings according to the work they have to do.

140
00:10:21,179 --> 00:10:24,293
Some money is needed right now, some years later.

141
00:10:24,293 --> 00:10:26,628
Keeping both in one place

142
00:10:26,628 --> 00:10:30,130
is like opening every lock with the same key.

143
00:10:30,130 --> 00:10:37,362
Second step, work out your real return yourself every year. Look at the interest,

144
00:10:37,362 --> 00:10:43,936
subtract the tax, and think about how much your household expenses have gone up.

145
00:10:43,936 --> 00:10:48,538
If what's left is very small,

146
00:10:48,538 --> 00:10:53,140
then at least do ask questions.

147
00:10:53,140 --> 00:10:58,423
Third step, understand other options for long-term goals. Like PPF,

148
00:10:58,423 --> 00:11:04,186
which is a government scheme and currently gives 7.1 percent interest per year.

149
00:11:04,186 --> 00:11:08,989
Every option has its own lock-in, risk and tax.

150
00:11:08,989 --> 00:11:10,910
First understand, then think.

151
00:11:10,910 --> 00:11:13,053
This is not investment advice.

152
00:11:13,053 --> 00:11:16,481
Before putting money anywhere, look at your needs,

153
00:11:16,481 --> 00:11:18,195
age and risk.

154
00:11:18,195 --> 00:11:22,052
If needed, talk to a qualified advisor.

155
00:11:22,052 --> 00:11:28,480
The only aim is that you can see the truth behind the number on the receipt.

156
00:11:28,480 --> 00:11:31,465
That night Papa opened the file,

157
00:11:31,465 --> 00:11:36,441
and for the first time kept the vegetable bill next to the receipt.

158
00:11:36,441 --> 00:11:41,914
He looked at both, and said softly, being safe and growing

159
00:11:41,914 --> 00:11:46,890
are different things. Nobody told me this earlier.

160
00:11:46,890 --> 00:11:49,125
Now, one simple question for you.

161
00:11:49,125 --> 00:11:53,148
Where is your household's biggest savings kept?

162
00:11:53,148 --> 00:11:58,065
In an FD or somewhere else? Write it in the comments in one word.

163
00:11:58,065 --> 00:12:00,300
I read every reply.

164
00:12:00,300 --> 00:12:06,844
In the next video, another story from home. Gold,

165
00:12:06,844 --> 00:12:15,569
which is kept somewhere in every mother's cupboard.

166
00:12:15,569 --> 00:12:21,385
Does it really protect us from rising prices,

167
00:12:21,385 --> 00:12:26,475
or is that also a sweet misunderstanding?

168
00:12:26,475 --> 00:12:30,110
See you in the next story.
